# CG

Display name is **CG** (broadcast Character Generator). Keep it. Do **not** rename to Overlay, Graphics, GFX, Live, Board, or Item.

This is the locked vocabulary for code, UI copy, DB, routes, and the subdomain. If a new Element needs a payload key, add it under `payload` jsonb — do not invent a parallel table or a second token scheme.

| Surface | Locked name |
|---|---|
| Launcher / `tyapp_app_feature.name` | `CG` |
| Route | `/cg` (`/cg/list`, `/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/:id`, `/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId`) |
| Overlay path | `/o/:token` on the CG host; fallback `/cg-live/:token` on Jaxfr |
| Subdomain | `cg` → `https://cg.tszyin.com` / `http://cg.localhost:4200` |
| Code | `features/cg/`, `apps/cg/` (overlay), `core/domains/cg/` |
| Panel files | `cg-package-edit.*` (skeleton is `*-edit`; the page is still Panel) |
| Layer desk | `cg-layer-edit.*` nested on the Panel at `/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId` (same right column as tiles — not a second page) |

## UI words

| Word | Means | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Package** | One look to use together | CH36, News SNG |
| **Element** | Kind in the catalog (code registry `CG_ELEMENT_CATALOG`) | Logo, Clock, Ticker |
| **Layer** | One instance inside a Package | CH36's Logo |
| **Panel** | This Package's operator page | Left Package (main), right Layers |
| **Output** | OBS URL (full-frame transparent Stage) | Package Output (default), Layer Output |
| **Stage** | 16:9 canvas | Tile thumbs, On air / Pending, overlay |
| **On air** | What OBS has (last Save, or live in Direct) | Monitor(s) in the left column |
| **Pending** | Unsaved draft mix (**Studio mode** only) | Save promotes it to On air |
| **Direct** | OBS-style: edit Program live | One On air monitor; auto-save to air |
| **Studio mode** | OBS Studio Mode: Preview then Program | Pending \| On air; Save to air |

**Channel / Source** stay on the Package as `role`. Clock is not Timer. Overlay is the public page implementation, not a product noun. Welcome → CG and every CG subpage (list / Panel) skip the Jaxfr page crossfade — instant swap, no 200ms fade. Other Jaxfr features keep the Aero transition. UI copy is **sentence case** (no `text-transform: uppercase` kickers/buttons). **Studio mode** (edit) is not the **Alpha / Dim** stage backdrop.

**Panel layout:** one page, two columns. Left is the **Package** (main): header (Back + Package only), then **monitor section** (Studio mode switch + Take/Create + On air status, then Pending|On air or single On air), then Name / Role / Appear / Look, then a **bottom footer** with Backdrop (Alpha | Dim) on the left and Delete package / Copy OBS URL on the right (no URL text shown). Right is **Layers** (catalog + tiles + selected Layer desk). Click the selected tile again to close the desk. Package title is heavier than Layers.

**Edit mode (per package, localStorage `cg-package-edit-mode:{id}`):**
- **Studio mode** ON (default): two monitors Pending \| On air on the **Package** column. Package mix waits for **Take**: name, role, Appear, Package Look, Layer existence / On-Off / z-order. **Layer desk is always Direct** — layout, Layer Look, image, News/Show, and cue write through to DB + On air immediately (debounced), even while Package Studio is on. Subtitle cue stays the live path it already was.
- **Studio mode** OFF (= Direct): Package column one On air monitor. Package mix also auto-saves (debounced) + Realtime broadcast. **Take** hidden once the package exists (first **Create** still needed). Turning Studio mode off with unsaved dirty promotes immediately.
- Workflow to hide mid-edit from air: Package Off → **Take** → edit Layer (live but Off) → On → **Take**. Skipping Take after Off means layout edits can still hit OBS while visible — accepted risk; watch Package **On air** (right).

**Always desktop on Panel only:** Panel (`/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/…`) locks the viewport to `width=1280` and `min-width: 1280px`. Phone and tablet keep the same 3-pane (pinch-zoom / horizontal pan) — do not add a stacked `@media` reflow. **List** uses normal responsive width like Attendance. Overlay `/o` and `/cg-live` stay `width=device-width`. Unlock the viewport when leaving Panel.

**No fixed palette — CG follows the operator's own Aero/Material + light/dark choice:** an earlier pass gave CG admin a fixed "broadcast console" identity (`_cg-theme.scss`); that was reverted (2026-09-24) after live review — the user wants the traditional skeuomorphic 3D "Windows 7 Aero / iOS 6" button look for themselves, but their partner prefers flat Material, and the app's existing per-user `visual_theme`/`color_mode` toggle (`UserPreferenceService`/`ThemeService`) already resolves that tension app-wide. CG does not need — and must not reintroduce — a third, fixed identity. `_cg-theme.scss` and its `console-light`/`console-dark` mixins are deleted; do not recreate them.

**Buttons are real Angular Material components, not hand-rolled `<button class="cg-btn">`:** action/toggle buttons in CG use `mat-stroked-button` / `mat-flat-button` with `.cg-seg-btn` for content groups (Channel/Source, Fade/Cut, Color/B&W, Inherit/Color/B&W, News/Show, Cue Fade/Cut, Alpha/Dim). **Studio mode** is a labeled `.cg-switch` in the Package header (not a second "Studio" segment). Sentence case labels — no uppercase transform. Aero/Material look comes from `_aero-controls.scss`. File-picker exception and Layer `.cg-switch` On/Off stay as before. Back is a plain circular `<a class="cg-back">`.

**No global toolbar:** `<app-toolbar>` is hidden for CG **Panel** paths (`/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/…`) via `isCgPanelPath()`. **List** (`/cg`, `/cg/list`) uses the normal AppToolbar through `HeaderService` — same pattern as Attendance (title, back to Welcome, Refresh, New package). Panel keeps Back / Studio mode / Take inline.

## Tables and columns (final)

`tyapp_cg_package` PK `tb_tyapp_cgpk_id` (seq `tb_tyapp_cgpk_seq_no`):

`name`, `role` (`channel` \| `source`), `public_token`, `duration_ms` (`0` = cut, default `400` = fade), `look` (`color` \| `mono`), `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`

`tyapp_cg_layer` PK `tb_tyapp_cgly_id` (seq `tb_tyapp_cgly_seq_no`):

`package_id` → package PK, `element_type`, `public_token`, `layout` jsonb, `payload` jsonb, `visible` (On/Off), `look` (`inherit` \| `color` \| `mono`; default `inherit` = Package Look), `sort_order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`

Layout jsonb: `x`, `y`, `unit` (`percent` \| `px`), `anchor`, `scale`, `width`, `height`. Logo `scale` is a CSS transform of the box. Subtitle `scale` only multiplies type size (`1` = ffmpeg FontSize 16.1 / PlayRes 288, about 5.6% of frame height); Show preset Scale 1 is about 7.2% of frame height. The caption stays inside `width` and wraps. Overlay uses `vh` so Browser Source gets on-air size even when `cqh` does not. News look is white fill, regular weight, `ScaleY` 1.11, `Spacing` 1.68. Black outline is a **behind** `-webkit-text-stroke` copy (fill sits on top). Do not put stroke and fill on the same span — OBS CEF has no `paint-order`, and 8-way `text-shadow` makes a jagged octagon around CJK. Show is larger, slightly gold, thicker behind-stroke. Latin runs use Segoe UI / Arial; CJK stays 華康中黑體 / JhengHei.

Logo payload jsonb: `imageUrl` (http(s) or app path such as `/icons/3d/apps.png` — **never** a `data:image` base64 string), `fileName`. "Choose local image" uploads PNG/WebP to the public Storage bucket `cg-logo` (`CgService.uploadLogoImage`) and stores only the public URL. Overlay used to poll `tyapp_cg_get_output_by_token` every 300ms forever; embedding the file in `payload` re-transmitted it on every poll (uncached PostgREST egress). Overlay now subscribes to Realtime broadcast `cg-output:{token}` (Panel sends on Save / live cue) and only hits that RPC on connect plus a 30s safety poll. Additive SQL: `supabase/sql/cg-logo-storage.sql`. Do not drop `tyapp_cg_*` tables for this.

Subtitle payload jsonb: `lines` (string[]), `index` (`number` \| `null` = blank / off air), `cursor` (last clicked row; kept when Blank), `style.preset` (`news` \| `show`; default `news`), `transition.duration_ms` (cue crossfade; `0` = cut, default `400`). This is **not** Package Appear.

Tokens share one `/o/:token` space (unique across both tables in practice). Do not add a token table.

RPCs: `tyapp_cg_package_soft_delete_single_record`, `tyapp_cg_layer_soft_delete_single_record`, `tyapp_cg_get_output_by_token`.

**Save** (Studio mode) writes the Package and applies it to Output. **Direct** auto-saves the same payload on each change (quiet toast). Each Layer **fades in or out on its own** using the Package `duration_ms` (`0` = cut). Layers that did not change stay put — turning Weather On does not blink an already-On Logo. Panel tile order is Stage **z-order** (first tile behind, last in front); drag to reorder, then Save (Studio) or auto-save (Direct).

**Host vs inner:** Package / Panel owns mix — which Layers exist, On/Off, z-order, OBS URL, **Appear** (Fade / Cut + `duration_ms` for the whole Layer going on or off), and **Package Look** as a master bus. Package B&W greys **every** Layer. Package Color lets a Layer set Inherit / Color / B&W (B&W = that Layer grey). Layer Color cannot punch out of a B&W Package. Layer desk does **not** have its own Appear. Cue crossfade, News / Show, layout, and later inner animation live on the Layer (`payload.transition.duration_ms` for cue). Package Cut must not force cue to cut.

**On air / Pending:**
- **Studio mode:** two small 16:9 Stages — **Pending left**, **On air right**. On air = last Save (OBS). Pending = draft. Save copies Pending onto On air. New unsaved Package: On air empty.
- **Direct:** one On air Stage (draft === air). Auto-save + broadcast on change.
- Live cue (Up / Down / Blank / Paste / Load) **and Cue Fade / Cut** always update On air immediately in both modes. Alpha / Dim backdrop toggle lives under **Backdrop** in the left footer (Package) and on the Layer desk.

**Save scope:**
- **Studio mode:** **Take** applies name, role, Appear, Package Look, and every Layer's existence / On-Off / z-order — not instant. Layer desk content (layout, Layer Look, image, News/Show) and subtitle cue already write through without Take.
- **Direct:** those same Package mix fields auto-save (debounced ~450ms) so OBS matches the Panel. Layer content still uses its own persist path when Studio is on; in Direct, full package autosave covers layers too.

**Layer desk monitors:** always a single **On air** preview for that one Layer (Layer is always Direct — not a second Studio switch). Own local Alpha/Dim backdrop; does not replace Package monitors. Package Look/Appear on that preview follow last Take (On air package) when Studio is on.

Greyscale is per-layer host filter with Package `duration_ms`; it must not change z-order.

**Subtitle cue is the live exception:** Up / Down / click / Paste / Load .txt or .srt patches only `lines` / `index` / `cursor` immediately (no Package Save). Cue Fade / Cut patches `payload.transition.duration_ms` the same way (`0` = cut, default `400`) — it is **not** Package Appear, and it does **not** wait for Save. Unsaved News/Show must not leak to OBS. Overlay gets cue via Realtime broadcast (plus a 30s RPC safety poll) and shows `lines[index]`. Cue changes **crossfade** with that Layer duration; this is inside the caption, not Layer On/Off opacity. `index = null` is blank air; `cursor` stays on the last clicked row so Down continues from there and Up puts it back. SRT import strips sequence numbers and timestamps; each cue becomes one queue line. Subtitle desk shows Cue Fade/Cut next to Up / Down / Blank, then Scale / Y / Width (bottom-center, `%`), plus News / Show. Logo still has full X/Y/Width/Scale/Anchor/Unit.

**Copy Layer** INSERTs a new row into another Package: new PK, new `public_token` (never share the OBS URL), `index = null`. Additive SQL: `supabase/sql/cg-layer-look.sql`.

Do not revive `tyapp_cg_slot` or `component_type`.
